  <section class="trust-benefits" aria-labelledby="benefitsTitle">
    <div class="trust-section-head"><p class="section-kicker">A calmer everyday browser</p><h2 id="benefitsTitle">The essentials, within reach.</h2></div>
    <article><span class="trust-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Find your way</h3><p>Navigation, search and tab switching share a compact island in a slim band above the page. Open its panel for the Quick Switcher or a slash command.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/island">Explore navigation ↗</a></article>
    <article><span class="trust-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Block the known noise</h3><p>Blanc Blocker uses bundled EasyList and EasyPrivacy rules at the network layer. Turn it off for a site when needed. No blocker can stop every tracker.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/ad-blocking">Explore blocking ↗</a></article>
    <article><span class="trust-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Keep tabs manageable</h3><p>Name your groups, reopen recently closed tabs and let inactive tabs go quiet to reclaim memory. Patron adds saved Named Workspaces.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features">Explore tab management ↗</a></article>
    <article><span class="trust-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Keep your 1Password logins close</h3><p>On macOS, fill matching logins from your installed 1Password app and account. Enable the built-in integration in Settings, then press ⌥⌘P on a login form.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/1password">Set up 1Password ↗</a></article>
  </section>
  <section class="trust-explain" aria-labelledby="trustTitle">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">How Blanc works</p><h2 id="trustTitle">A closer look at Blanc.</h2><p>Explore the technology behind Blanc, how updates work and the services it connects to. Fresh setup preselects search suggestions and usage measurement. These optional connections start only after you save your choices; you can turn either off before continuing or later in Settings.</p></div>
    <div class="trust-explain-links"><a href="/how-it-works">Technology and updates <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/how-it-works#connections">Connections and privacy controls <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/features/security">Security and verified releases <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/privacy">Privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-faq" aria-labelledby="home-faq-title">
    <div class="home-faq-head"><p class="section-kicker">A few useful answers</p><h2 id="home-faq-title">Before you download.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/faq">Read the full FAQ ↗</a></div>
    <div class="home-faq-list faq-list">
      <details><summary><span>Is Blanc based on Chromium?</span><svg class="faq-toggle" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8h10" /><path class="faq-toggle-vertical" d="M8 3v10" /></svg></summary><p>Yes. Chromium renders websites, Electron bundles the engine and desktop runtime, and Blanc supplies the browser interface and features.</p></details>
      <details><summary><span>Does Blanc work with 1Password?</span><svg class="faq-toggle" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8h10" /><path class="faq-toggle-vertical" d="M8 3v10" /></svg></summary><p>Yes, on macOS. Blanc has built-in login fill for your installed 1Password app and account. It is off by default and fills only when you ask. Windows and Linux do not currently offer this integration. <a href="/features/1password">See setup and shortcuts.</a></p></details>
      <details><summary><span>Does Blanc send usage data?</span><svg class="faq-toggle" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8h10" /><path class="faq-toggle-vertical" d="M8 3v10" /></svg></summary><p>If you save Help improve Blanc as on, packaged builds send pseudonymous launch and fixed feature-use events to a Blanc-owned Cloudflare collector, with an optional Google Analytics mirror. No URLs, searches or page contents are in those events. <a href="/how-it-works#connections">See the connections and controls.</a></p></details>
      <details><summary><span>Is Blanc free and open source?</span><svg class="faq-toggle" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8h10" /><path class="faq-toggle-vertical" d="M8 3v10" /></svg></summary><p>Browsing essentials and ordinary tab groups are free. Active Patron adds the ability to create saved Named Workspaces. Blanc’s own code is MIT licensed; names, logos and third-party material have separate terms.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>
